Z||000005||bHooper||07-11-2000||09:42 AM||||Cooter... you have to be right on with that.  I think it was Speed Buggy.<P>Man, wasn't TV great when all the producers and creators would use mind altering drugs to creat childrens shows?!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Remember the show with Ruth Buzzy and Jim Neighbors as the Robots from outer space?  Or how about the one with "Gilligan" as a astronaut, and his pet with the horn for a nose?<P>Of course, H&R Puff-n-Stuff was the king of the "pot influenced" shows.  They still show that on sunday mornings, sometimes.<P>And then there was  Marshall, Will and Holly... oh Holly, oh Holly.... <A HREF="http://www.landofthelost.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.landofthelost.com/</A> <BR>oh Holly... oh, I need to go now, my shrink is calling me.......<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000006||Sleestak||07-11-2000||01:15 PM||||Thanks for the site plug, I saw this site pop up in my site stats already, and I saw you had some questions about Krofft shows so I hope its OK if I jump in here and answer you.<P>The show about the car with the magic horn was call "Wonderbug", it was a live action show by Sid and Marty Krofft that ran from September 11, 1976 - September2, 1978. You have the Schlepcar, honk the horn, you get Wonderbug.<P>The show with Jim Neighbors and Ruth Buzzi is called "Lost Saucer" and the one with Gilligan and his strange pet is "Far Out Space Nuts."<P>And frightenly enough, all these shows, plus Land of the Lost are currently available on video and some on DVD from Rhino Home video. You can search Amazon or if you visit my site I have links and descriptions of all the videos and DVDS.<P>If you have any more Krofft questions, I'm ready!<P>George<BR>Webmaster -  <A HREF="http://Landofthelost.com" TARGET=_blank>Landofthelost.com</A> <P><p>[This message has been edited by Sleestak (edited 07-11-2000).]||||reg||12
Z||000007||My7Fieros||07-12-2000||02:51 AM||||SLEESTAK, YOU ARE THE GREATEST!!!!!!!! Do you know Ive been trying to find out the name of that show for the past 20 years..NOBODY has ever heard of it!! Thank you!!!! Now, do you know of a website where I can find anything about that show Wonderbug?<p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 07-12-2000).]||||reg||1
